---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../../styles/global.css";
---

<Layout
	title="Mean of Grouped Data | Statistics | Class 10 | The Concepts Adda"
	description="Learn how to calculate Mean of grouped data using Direct Method, Assumed Mean Method, and Step-Deviation Method for Class 10 NCERT Mathematics."
>
	<main class="lesson-page">
		<div class="lesson-container">
			<a href="/statistics" class="back-link">
				<span class="back-arrow">←</span>
				<span>Back to Statistics</span>
			</a>

			<!-- LESSON HEADER -->
			<section class="lesson-header">
				<div class="lesson-number">01</div>
				<div class="lesson-header-copy">
					<div class="lesson-label">LESSON 01 · CLASS 10 MATHEMATICS (NCERT)</div>
					<h1>Mean of <span>Grouped Data</span></h1>
					<p>
						Master calculating the mean (average) of grouped frequency distributions using the Direct Method, Assumed Mean Method, and Step-Deviation Method.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- CONTENT LAYOUT -->
			<section class="content-layout">
				<article class="lesson-content">

					<!-- 01 · CLASS MARK DEFINITION -->
					<div class="topic-label">01 · CLASS MARK</div>
					<h2>Class Mark (xᵢ)</h2>
					<p>
						For grouped data, the central representative value of each class interval is called the <strong>class mark (xᵢ)</strong>:
					</p>

					<div class="formula-box">
						<strong>Class Mark xᵢ = (Upper Class Limit + Lower Class Limit) / 2</strong>
					</div>

					<!-- 02 · THREE METHODS TO FIND MEAN -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">02 · THREE METHODS</div>
					<h2>Formulas for Finding Mean (x̄)</h2>

					<div class="summary-list">
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>1. Direct Method</span>
							<div>
								<p><strong>Direct Method</strong></p>
								<span style="color:#64748b; font-size:14px;"><strong>x̄ = Σfᵢxᵢ / Σfᵢ</strong> (Best when values of fᵢ and xᵢ are small).</span>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>2. Assumed Mean</span>
							<div>
								<p><strong>Assumed Mean Method</strong></p>
								<span style="color:#64748b; font-size:14px;"><strong>x̄ = a + (Σfᵢdᵢ / Σfᵢ)</strong> where <em>dᵢ = xᵢ - a</em> (a is assumed mean).</span>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>3. Step-Deviation</span>
							<div>
								<p><strong>Step-Deviation Method</strong></p>
								<span style="color:#64748b; font-size:14px;"><strong>x̄ = a + (Σfᵢuᵢ / Σfᵢ) × h</strong> where <em>uᵢ = (xᵢ - a)/h</em> and <em>h</em> is class size.</span>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 03 · SOLVED NCERT EXAMPLE -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">03 · SOLVED NCERT EXAMPLE</div>
					<h2>Step-by-Step Problem Solving</h2>

					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">EXAMPLE 1</span>
							<h3>Find the mean marks obtained by 30 students in a mathematics test</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<p>Given distribution table:</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								Class Interval &nbsp;|&nbsp; Frequency fᵢ &nbsp;|&nbsp; Class Mark xᵢ &nbsp;|&nbsp; fᵢxᵢ<br/>
								10 - 25 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; 2 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; 17.5 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; 35.0<br/>
								25 - 40 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; 3 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; 32.5 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; 97.5<br/>
								40 - 55 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; 7 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; 47.5 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; 332.5<br/>
								55 - 70 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; 6 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; 62.5 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; 375.0<br/>
								70 - 85 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; 6 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; 77.5 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; 465.0<br/>
								85 - 100 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; 6 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; 92.5 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; 555.0<br/>
								-------------------------------------------------------------<br/>
								Total &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; Σfᵢ = 30 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; - &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; Σfᵢxᵢ = 1860.0
							</div>

							<p style="margin-top:14px;"><strong>Calculating Mean by Direct Method</strong>:</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								x̄ = Σfᵢxᵢ / Σfᵢ = 1860 / 30 = <strong>62.0</strong>
							</div>
							<p style="margin-top:10px;">Mean marks obtained by students is <strong>62</strong>.</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 04 · QUICK SUMMARY -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">04 · QUICK SUMMARY</div>
					<h2>Key Takeaways</h2>

					<div class="summary-list">
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>01</span>
							<p>Class mark xᵢ = <strong>(Upper Limit + Lower Limit) / 2</strong>.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>02</span>
							<p>Direct method formula: <strong>x̄ = Σfᵢxᵢ / Σfᵢ</strong>.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>03</span>
							<p>Assumed mean method reduces big numbers by using <strong>dᵢ = xᵢ - a</strong>.</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- LESSON NAVIGATION -->
					<div class="lesson-navigation">
						<a href="/statistics" class="previous-lesson">
							<span>←</span>
							<div>
								<small>OVERVIEW</small>
								<strong>Chapter Overview</strong>
							</div>
						</a>

						<a href="/statistics/mode-of-grouped-data" class="next-lesson">
							<div>
								<small>NEXT LESSON</small>
								<strong>Mode of Grouped Data</strong>
							</div>
							<span>→</span>
						</a>
					</div>
				</article>

